BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261015T235334Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53931703767885
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DESCRIPTION:This conference is made possible by the Congress of Graduate Students at Florida State University. \n\nKeynote Speakers:\nZoë Johnson King (Harvard University)\nDavid Shoemaker (Cornell University)\n\nAll events will take place at Dodd Hall Auditorium (DHA 103) unless otherwise noted. All graduate student talks will be roughly 25 minutes long\, followed by comments (~10 minutes)\, a response (~5 minutes)\, and a Q&A session (~10 minutes). Keynote addresses will include a talk followed by a Q&A session.\n\nSchedule\n\nAll events will take place at Dodd Hall Auditorium (DHA 103) unless otherwise noted.\n\nFRIDAY\, OCTOBER 16\n\n3:30–5:30 p.m. — KEYNOTE ADDRESS\n\nZoë Johnson King\, Harvard University\n“Aretaic Injustice”\n\nSATURDAY\, OCTOBER 17\n\n9:00 a.m. — Coffee and Refreshments\n\n9:30 a.m. — Yiqun Chen\, Simon Fraser University\n“Whose Wrong Is This?”\nComments by Asher Baumrin\n\n10:30 a.m. — Gabriel Maruchi\, Universidade Estadual de Campinas\n“Moral Luck and Contrastive Causation”\nComments by Minsu Kim\n\n11:30 a.m. — Samuel Delorme\, UC San Diego\n“Responsibility and Externalism About Capacities”\nComments by Micah Edvenson\n\n12:30–1:30 p.m. — Break\n\n1:30 p.m. — Max Ma\, Duke University\n“Culpability and Deliberation Without Ability”\nComments by Liam Jones\n\n2:30 p.m. — Zed Zhang\, Rutgers University\n“The Reverse Deep Self View”\nComments by Letícia Palazzo-Rodrigues\n\n3:30–5:30 p.m. — KEYNOTE ADDRESS\n\nDavid Shoemaker\, Cornell University\n“Pluralistic Praise: Its Nature\, Function(s)\, Worthiness\, and Reasons”
GEO:30.439803;-84.292645
LOCATION:Dodd Hall Auditorium (DHA)\, 103
SUMMARY:15th Annual Florida State University Free Will\, Moral Responsibility\, and Agency Conference
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/15th-annual-florida-state-university-free-will-moral-responsibility-and-agency-conference-864
CATEGORIES:Conferences
END:VEVENT
